From 5c2960adbef76958425bca83f43568771383f18f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aadi Takle <aadiatakle@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 16:29:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(exam-scoring): the residual null lambda is endogeneity,
 not the fit

E-200 corrected the guessing floor and left a null-cohort lambda of about
+0.009 that three banks in three domains and a grid with no items in it all
returned identically. That localised it to the estimator plus the targeting
loop but could not say which part, because freezing the difficulty removes two
things at once: the climb, and the climb's dependence on the child's answers.

Replaying each child's OWN adaptive difficulty path against an independent
answer stream separates them. Identical path, identical ability, identical
handover, only the dependence cut: +0.0085 becomes -0.0039 on the bank-free
grid at an unchanged 0.29-point climb. A rising ladder manufactures nothing,
and a steeper exogenous one manufactures less. The cause is that the served
difficulty is a function of the child's own earlier answers.

The first hypothesis is refuted in the wrong direction. Conditioning the fit
on served difficulty with a free coefficient - the shape of the pre-registered
Gate B statistic - roughly doubles the artifact, because difficulty was never
omitted from the fit, it is endogenous within it. Both standard finite-sample
bias corrections also move it up, so the residual is not that kind of bias,
and a conditional likelihood has nothing to add: a selection rule depending
only on the observed past is ignorable.

Add `scheduledTargetTheta`, which is handed a trial index and no responses, so
it cannot use them. Gate A on all four banks and the grid, 8 seeds x 400
children: null lambda 0.0085 -> -0.0033, 0.0097 -> -0.0019, 0.0092 -> -0.0021,
0.0087 -> -0.0027, 0.0166 -> 0.0063, a near-constant -0.011 everywhere.
Per-cell A1 reaches 8/8 on two banks.

NOT ADOPTED, because the price is larger than the bias. Mean posterior SE
widens about a third, A4 gets worse rather than better, and the share of blocks
where a band can be named at all falls 12 to 16 points on every pool whose
floor was already right. `nextTargetTheta` stays the default, nothing is wired
into the live block, no user-facing surface changes, and `--fix-probe` is
byte-identical to dev so the three published Gate A reports still reproduce.

D-206 is Proposed and states the trade for the owner. E-205 records the
attribution, every rejected candidate, the before/after, and the rate sweep
that shows the schedule's rate buys nothing on A1 and costs on everything else.
E-200's mechanism sentence is corrected in place; its figures stand.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
